        "created_at": "2024-11-07T07:36:52.116Z",
        "cooked": "<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://europe1.discourse-cdn.com/flex013/uploads/iitm/original/3X/5/4/542a2f30599f0bc5ce19257e4c623b72e1f68099.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/c0yuc9a6oqBVDRh2VU3t4uHgvtD.png?dl=1\" title=\"Untitled picture\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"><img src=\"https://europe1.discourse-cdn.com/flex013/uploads/iitm/original/3X/5/4/542a2f30599f0bc5ce19257e4c623b72e1f68099.png\" alt=\"Untitled picture\" data-base62-sha1=\"c0yuc9a6oqBVDRh2VU3t4uHgvtD\" width=\"500\" height=\"265\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">Untitled picture</span><span class=\"informations\">500×265 6.08 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div><br>\nThis question from GA of WK5 deems the 2nd option, which has a semicolon after each parenthesis as correct. Is this because of strict syntax criteria? Shouldn’t the 4th option be correct as well?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
