        "id": 553002,
        "name": "Sayan Ghosh",
        "username": "sayan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discourse.onlinedegree.iitm.ac.in/sayan/{size}/112713_2.png",
        "created_at": "2024-11-07T09:26:11.154Z",
        "cooked": "<p>To create a subshell, we put the commands inside one pair of parenthesis <code>( echo $BASH_SUBSHELL )</code>.</p>\n<p>Recall that the syntax for executing arithmetic in bash also uses parentheses <code>(( 5 + 6 ))</code>.</p>\n<p>If you do not provide the semicolons, bash thinks it is the arithmetic evaluation instead of subshell.</p>\n<p>To make it clear that it is successive subshelling (3 times), we need to separate the parenthesis from each other using semicolon.</p>",
