  "accepted_answer": {
    "post_number": 2,
    "username": "sayan",
    "name": null,
    "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discourse.onlinedegree.iitm.ac.in/sayan/{size}/112713_2.png",
    "excerpt": "<p>To create a subshell, we put the commands inside one pair of parenthesis <code>( echo $BASH_SUBSHELL )</code>.</p>\n<p>Recall that the syntax for executing arithmetic in bash also uses parentheses <code>(( 5 + 6 ))</code>.</p>\n<p>If you do not provide the semicolons, bash thinks it is the arithmetic evaluation instead of subshell.</p>\n<p>To make it clear that it is successive subshelling (3 times), we need to separate the parenthesis from each other using semicolon.</p>",
    "accepter_name": null,
    "accepter_username": "Louis"
  },
